commit 48f38b60d97b0e5d95ded6b4293038a4509625ce
Author: Nick Hung <nick@andestech.com>
Date:   Thu May 7 09:21:09 2026 +0800

    behavioral: ResumeDriver Tier-A V-CSR restore with PB fallback

    When HYBRID_FLAG_V is set, resume() now restores vstart (0x008),
    vxsat (0x009), vxrm (0x00A), vcsr (0x00F), and mstatus.VS (when
    non-zero) via Abstract Commands before the GPR loop.  If the DM
    signals cmderr on any abstract CSR write, write_csr_abstract_or_pb()
    clears the sticky error, stages the value in x5 (t0) via an abstract
    GPR write, and issues a one-instruction Program Buffer (csrrw x0, csr,
    x5).  x5 is overwritten by the GPR restore loop that follows, so the
    scratch use is invisible to QEMU2.

    - Fix pre-existing test bug: mtvec (0x305) was in the "should NOT
      program" exclusion list but the driver correctly writes it; removed.
      Also removed HYBRID_FLAG_V from that test state (scope is FP/PMP).
    - RecordingBus gains abstractcs_queue (std::deque) for per-read
      sequencing of the abstractcs register.
    - Three new tests: abstract writes for all four V CSRs appear; V CSR
      writes precede GPR writes; PB fallback fires on cmderr.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

